course: dictionary
lesson: 2676
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Diamond» is one of them. A diamond can be a sparkling stone, a shape with four equal sides, a suit of playing cards, or a field in baseball. Context clues tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «She wore a diamond ring on her finger.» The ring and the finger are your clues. A ring is jewellery, so a diamond here is the sparkling stone. Now try the meaning in the sentence: «She wore a sparkling stone ring on her finger.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The kite had a diamond shape, with four equal sides.» Here the words four equal sides tell you that diamond means a shape, which maths calls a rhombus. A shape with four equal sides is not a stone, so the clues point you to the right meaning every time.
explain: When two meanings seem possible, read the whole sentence and ask what it is about. Jewellery, maths, cards and baseball all have their own clues. If you are still not sure, check the dictionary.
fact: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is right.
fact: «Diamond» means a very hard, clear, sparkling precious stone.
fact: In maths, a diamond shape is a rhombus: four equal sides, standing on one of its corners.
fact: Diamonds is one of the four suits in a pack of cards, shown with red diamond shapes.
fact: In baseball, the diamond is the field with four bases. Diamonds and pencil graphite are both pure carbon, though their atoms are arranged differently.
exercise: «She wore a diamond ring on her finger.» What is a diamond in this sentence? | *A very hard, clear, sparkling precious stone | A field with four bases | A kind of fruit | A shape with four equal sides
exercise: «The kite had a diamond shape, with four equal sides.» In maths, what is a diamond shape called? | A circle | *A rhombus | A triangle | A cube
exercise: Sam picks the seven of diamonds from the pack. What does diamonds mean here? | A sparkling stone for a ring | *One of the four suits in a pack of cards | A baseball field | A kind of kite
test: «Diamond and pencil graphite are both pure carbon; the atoms are arranged differently.» What is the same about them? | They are both found on a baseball field | *They are both made of pure carbon | They are both playing cards | They are both shapes with four sides
test: The baseball coach shouts, «Run to the diamond!» What is the diamond here? | One of the suits in a pack of cards | A shape in maths | *The field with four bases | A stone for a ring
exam: «Ten courtiers ornamented with diamonds» means the courtiers were decorated with | *sparkling precious stones | four-sided shapes | baseball bases | playing cards
